      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RED MINK (9) will be having her second outing after doing some work to lead at Tatura. She has since trialled well and after being fancied at that first run, you would think things would work out better here. Some important guiding gear changes are a benefit as well. TOSEN FURY (2) resumes after some wet track efforts. He likes to race up on the speed and both runs here have been sound. He'll be better this time around. CARLOW ROSE (3) kept improving from run to run and now has a good fitness base. Would love a damp surface. NEWS SCOOP (5) has to be one to note after two Victorian runs. Only had one trial to be ready but must go in. KUTINA BAY (4) is a debut runner as a 5yo so they must have persisted for a reason.",
